<title>SPAIN: SWIMMING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP LONG-DISTANCE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP LONG-DISTANCE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE, Spain 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of the men's</p>
<p>25-kilometre long-distance event at the European championships</p>
<p>on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Alexei Akatiev (Russia) five hours five minutes zero</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p>2 equal. Stephane Lecat (France) 5:08:36</p>
<p>2 equal. Christoph Wandratsch (Germany) 5:08:36</p>
<p>4. Claudio Gargaro (Italy) 5:09:11</p>
<p>5. Yuri Kudinov (Russia) 5:09:58</p>
<p>6. David Meca (Spain) 5:11:10</p>
<p>7. Nicolas Knap (France) 5:12:19</p>
<p>8. Fabrizio Pescatori (Italy) 5:12:23</p>
<p>9. David Royo (Spain) 5:14:21</p>
<p>10. Andre Wilde (Germany) 5:14:58</p>
<p>11. Christian Hansmann (Germany) 5:27:20</p>
<p>12. Justin Palfrey (Britain) 5:27:52</p>
<p>13. Rostislav Vitek (Czech Republic) 5:31:20</p>
<p>14. Trpimir Kutle (Croatia) 5:40:18</p>
<p>15. Robert Dinka (Slovakia) 5:45:49</p>
<p>16. Norbert Csendes (Hungary) 6:00:49</p>
<p>Did not finish: Fabio Fusi (Italy), Michal Spacek (Czech</p>
<p>Republic).</p>
</text>
